cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use navalign, please cite it as below."
type: software
title: "navalign: navigation-alignment scoring for coding-agent traces"
abstract: >-
  navalign scores how directly a coding agent's exploration reached the code that the real fix
  changed. Given a task's code graph, its reference patch and an ATIF trace, it reports
  file-level (S_file, focus) and node-level (S_node) navigation scores and per-step distances, and
  breaks each run's outcome into never found / found but not edited / edited but failed / passed.
authors:
  - given-names: Kai
    alias: vlyot
version: 0.1.0
license: Apache-2.0
repository-code: "https://github.com/vlyot/navalign"
keywords:
  - coding agents
  - agent evaluation
  - code localization
  - SWE-bench
  - ATIF
